{"id":"pool-garden-view","version":1,"category":"amenity","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for pool and garden outlook.","title":"Pool and garden outlook","combinations":"Limestone basin-like enclosure and deck; water remains the dedicated rectangular surface primitive.","placement":"Orient the long view from terrace across the basin toward an assumed garden edge.","principles":"Do not invent a surveyed horizon or use water as the only landscape.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, wall, water. No hydraulic systems, filtration, waterproofing, hot-water equipment or arbitrary curved pools.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Checked primitive names against the direct-scene contract; individually curated conceptual relationships, not external research or a regulation."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","water"],"materials":"Limestone basin-like enclosure and deck; water remains the dedicated rectangular surface primitive.","supports":"Construct a bottom below water, four connected perimeter edges and a dry approach deck; disclose absent services.","unsupported":"No hydraulic systems, filtration, waterproofing, hot-water equipment or arbitrary curved pools."}}
{"id":"dining-transition","version":1,"category":"programme","when":"Meals connecting indoor and outdoor rooms.","title":"Dining between kitchen and garden","combinations":"Use a shaded outdoor extension.","placement":"Place dining beside kitchen and terrace doors with clear passing space.","principles":"Avoid making the table the only circulation route.","capabilities":"plate, wall openings, entrance or glazing and roof; furniture clearance needs review.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Operation availability checked against the direct-scene contract. Design guidance is conceptual curation, not a verified regulation or external research."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"plate, wall openings, entrance or glazing and roof; furniture clearance needs review. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"outdoor-reading-nook","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for sheltered garden reading nook.","title":"Sheltered garden reading nook","combinations":"Timber shade members and limestone outdoor paving; ivory supports keep a quiet background.","placement":"Use a modest floor and supported shade beside a quiet room threshold.","principles":"Do not add a detached pavilion simply to increase complexity.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, roof, volume. No planting generator, curved pergolas, rain drainage or microclimate simulation.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Checked primitive names against the direct-scene contract; individually curated conceptual relationships, not external research or a regulation."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","roof","volume"],"materials":"Timber shade members and limestone outdoor paving; ivory supports keep a quiet background.","supports":"Construct connected walking plates with explicit shade supports and actual room thresholds nearby.","unsupported":"No planting generator, curved pergolas, rain drainage or microclimate simulation."}}
{"id":"legacy-recipe-21d1571a-86f7-4226-bb31-33b2677f13ec","version":1,"category":"climate-site","when":"Existing planting recipe; original compatible scales: family, luxury.","title":"Modern Tropical Poolside Planting Garden 01","combinations":"[{\"kind\":\"requires\",\"note\":\"along one or more non-access pool edges\",\"target\":\"pool\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"visible from covered outdoor living areas\",\"target\":\"terrace\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"screen service edges without blocking circulation\",\"target\":\"outdoor-kitchen\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"uplight selected palms and specimen foliage\",\"target\":\"lighting\"},{\"kind\":\"conflicts\",\"note\":\"avoid dense planting at vehicle sightlines\",\"target\":\"driveway\"}]","placement":"Layer palms, broadleaf understory, and low groundcover from back to front. Frame ocean or garden views rather than forming a continuous visual wall. Keep pool access paths and emergency egress clear. Use salt-tolerant species on exposed beach sites. Cluster boulders and sculptural plants as deliberate focal points. Conceal pool equipment and boundary edges with dense evergreen foliage. Maintain a restrained palette of repeated tropical species for a modern composition.","principles":"Adapt approved guidance to the brief. Parameter options: [{\"key\":\"bedDepth\",\"max\":5,\"min\":1.2,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":2.4},{\"key\":\"canopyPalmSpacing\",\"max\":8,\"min\":3.5,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":5.5},{\"key\":\"understoryPlantDensity\",\"max\":5,\"min\":1.5,\"unit\":\"plants/m²\",\"value\":2.8},{\"key\":\"groundcoverCoverage\",\"max\":95,\"min\":40,\"unit\":\"%\",\"value\":72},{\"key\":\"featureBoulderCount\",\"max\":16,\"min\":0,\"unit\":\"count\",\"value\":5},{\"key\":\"pathClearance\",\"max\":2,\"min\":0.9,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":1.2},{\"key\":\"accentLighting\",\"unit\":\"boolean\",\"value\":true},{\"key\":\"plantingCharacter\",\"unit\":\"string\",\"value\":\"layered-lush\",\"options\":[\"layered-lush\",\"sculptural-minimal\",\"coastal-resilient\"]}].","capabilities":"Required capabilities: . Check against the scene construction contract; approval does not implement capabilities.","sources":[{"reference":"library recipe 21d1571a-86f7-4226-bb31-33b2677f13ec","note":"Existing recipe approval; no new external verification.","kind":"repository","verified":false}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Required capabilities: . Check against the scene construction contract; approval does not implement capabilities. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"asymmetric-balance","version":1,"category":"composition","when":"An irregular programme or unequal views.","title":"Asymmetric balance","combinations":"Use repeated datums to unify unequal masses.","placement":"Balance a taller living volume with a longer low wing and a sheltered void.","principles":"Avoid random offsets.","capabilities":"plate, wall and independent roof sections; no visual-balance solver.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Operation availability checked against the direct-scene contract. Design guidance is conceptual curation, not a verified regulation or external research."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"plate, wall and independent roof sections; no visual-balance solver. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
